    "fileId": 22008,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Essential diagnostic criteria for refractory cytopenia of childhood</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Charlotte M. Niemeyer",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 703.3pt; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"938\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 3.5pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 65.5pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"87\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 212.6pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"283\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Erythropoiesis</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 212.6pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"283\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Granulopoiesis</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 212.6pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 3.5pt;\" width=\"283\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Megakaryopoiesis</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 65.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"87\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Bone marrow aspirate</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 212.6pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"283\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Dysplastic changes<sup>a</sup> and/or megaloblastoid changes</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 212.6pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"283\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Dysplastic changes<sup>b</sup> in &ge;&nbsp;10% of granulocytic precursors and neutrophils; &lt;&nbsp;5% blasts</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 212.6pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"283\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Unequivocal micromegakaryocytes; other dysplastic changes<sup>c</sup> in variable numbers</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 65.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"87\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Bone marrow biopsy</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 212.6pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"283\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">A few clusters of &ge;&nbsp;20&nbsp;erythroid precursors; arrested in maturation with increased numbers of proerythroblasts; increased mitotic count</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 212.6pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"283\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">No minimal diagnostic criteria</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 212.6pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"283\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Unequivocal micromegakaryocytes; immunohistochemistry is obligatory (CD61, CD41); other dysplastic changes<sup>c</sup> in variable numbers</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 65.5pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"87\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Peripheral blood</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 212.6pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"283\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 212.6pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"283\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Dysplastic changes<sup>b</sup> in &ge;&nbsp;10%&nbsp;of neutrophils</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 212.6pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"283\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>Erythroid dysplasia: abnormal nuclear lobulation, multinucleated cells, nuclear bridges. <sup>b</sup>Granulocytic dysplasia: pseudo&ndash;Pelger&ndash;Hu&euml;t cells, hypogranularity or agranularity, giant bands; in cases of severe neutropenia, this criterion may not be fulfilled.<sup> c</sup>Megakaryocytic dysplasia: variable size with separated nuclei or round nuclei; the absence of megakaryocytes does not rule out refractory cytopenia of childhood.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Note: The dysplasia criteria must be fulfilled in &ge;&nbsp;10% of cells in &ge;&nbsp;1&nbsp;lineage; in some cases, lesser degrees of dysplasia are present in 2&nbsp;or 3&nbsp;lineages.</p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 51478,
