    "title": "<p>Bone marrow findings in refractory cytopenia of childhood (RCC)</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Charlotte M. Niemeyer",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 697.9pt; border-collapse: collapse; \" border=\"0\" width=\"931\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.5pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 297.2pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"396\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Bone marrow biopsy</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 297.2pt; border: none; border-top: solid black 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"396\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Bone marrow aspirate</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><a name=\"_Hlk97629399\"></a><strong>Erythropoiesis</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 297.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"396\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Patchy distribution</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Left shift with increased numbers of proerythroblasts</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Increased mitotic count</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">In normocellular/hypercellular RCC: increase in erythropoiesis</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">In hypocellular RCC: a few clusters of &ge;&nbsp;20&nbsp;erythroid precursors</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 297.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"396\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Dysplastic changes with</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; \">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>abnormal nuclear segmentation</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; \">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>multinucleated cells</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; \">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>nuclear bridges</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Megaloblastoid changes (in some cases)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.5pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Granulopoiesis</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 297.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"396\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Marked decrease</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Left shift</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 297.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"396\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Pseudo&ndash;Pelger&ndash;Hu&euml;t anomaly</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Agranularity of cytoplasm</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Hypogranularity of cytoplasm</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Nuclear&ndash;cytoplasmic maturation defect</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Megakaryopoiesis</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 297.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"396\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Marked decrease or aplasia</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Dysplastic changes</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Micromegakaryocytes</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 297.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"396\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Micromegakaryocytes</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Multiple separated nuclei</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Small round nuclei</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\" page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 103.5pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"138\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Lymphocytes</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 297.2pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"396\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">May be increased focally or dispersed</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 297.2pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid black 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"396\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">May be increased</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  }
]